--- Surface ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
MotorEfficiencyInsights is implemented to parity with
web/src/features/driving/components/driving-dynamics/MotorEfficiencyInsights.tsx and verified headlessly
(71 new tests). The web component's three glass panels are reproduced natively:
  - Torque Distribution (lightning glyph): Avg Torque / Max Torque (Nm) + High Torque Time (%).
  - Throttle Behavior (gauge glyph): Avg Power (kW), a driving-style Badge (conservative=success /
    moderate=warning / aggressive=danger, derived from avg power via getThrottleStyle) and a power MetricBar
    (max 200 kW, empty label/sublabel so no stray "0.00" readout — the web regression is reproduced + guarded).
  - Motor Thermal (thermometer glyph): Avg / Max Motor Temp converted to the user's unit at the display
    boundary (the unit label already carries the degree sign — the "49.0°°C" doubling bug is guarded), plus a
    thermal Badge (raw-Celsius threshold: <100 good / <140 warm / else hot).
All six P2 states render (loading skeletons / ready / empty "No motor data recorded yet" per panel / error
QueryError with retry / stale chip / offline chip). The data adapter (computeMotorStats: torque/temp/power/
regen aggregation, high-torque %) is ported 1:1 and unit-tested. The view performs no HTTP — it binds a
WinUI-free Model projected by MotorEfficiencyInsightsProjection. All 17 web i18n keys (dynamics.*) resolve
through the i18n facade and already exist in Strings/{en,he,ar}/Resources.resw; the native-only error/stale
keys (dynamics.motorInsightsError / dynamics.motorInsightsErrorMessage / common.stale) resolve via the
ILocalizer English fallback, exactly as the sibling TemperatureGauges surface does. Narrator names are set on
the surface and every panel; entrances honour reduce-motion; diagnostics emit only
"view.opened slug=MotorEfficiencyInsights" (PII-safe).

